hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1491","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Shuaib told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yasar, that he heard Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you performs ablution and performs it well and completes it, then comes The mosque is only intended to be prayed in, without God looking forward to it just as the family of an absent person looks forward to his appearance.”"
